$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=rectintshl  LOC_AFTER=?

* The line-shift identity with a residue: if the boundary integral over every rectangle of height t is K and the two horizontal edge integrals tend to zero, the two vertical edge limits add up to K.  This is Carmichael.shift_lines_residue of DetectionShift.lean, with the improper integrals given as limits of the truncated ones.

